Theorem RL-19: thread-local values use non-atomic RC

  Preconditions:
    - RL-19 governs thread-local non-atomic RC per Annex E §AIMS
      Non-Atomic RC: "Thread-local values (no cross-thread escape) SHALL use
      non-atomic RC (plain load/store, not atomic CAS). Thread-locality
      derived from Locality + call-graph: no escape path crosses a thread
      boundary (spawn, channel, FFI) -> thread-local."
    - Signature ArcFunction x AimsStateMap -> ArcFunction per
      the canonical proof notation:264; discharged against the sec-01
      Realization.proof sorry obligation.
    - Thread-locality is the RL-18a-derived property (Locality + call-graph),
      NOT a separate per-variable escape dimension.
    - Shipped: target-system rule (ori_repr apply_thread_local_arc stubbed per
      repr.md); realize/decide.rs consumes Locality.
    - depends-on RL-18a (Locality as escape SSOT for the thread-locality
      derivation).

  Soundness property:
    Forall value v whose escape paths never cross a thread boundary
    (thread-local):

      (P1) Atomicity decision: RL-19 emits non-atomic RC (plain load/store)
           for v.

      (P2) Soundness: a thread-local value's reference count is only ever
           mutated by the owning thread, so no data race on the count is
           possible — plain (non-atomic) load/store is correct, and avoids
           the atomic-CAS overhead.

    RL-19 refines plain ARC (which would use atomic RC everywhere) by using
    non-atomic RC whenever the value provably never crosses a thread boundary.

  Proof obligation:
    Constructive discharge by the case_analysis engine.

    Part (P1/P2) — thread-local atomicity:
      The verifier confirms a FunctionLocal value and a HeapEscaping value
      that does NOT cross a thread boundary are both classified thread-local
      (derives_thread_shared = false) and both receive non-atomic RC.
      Coverage gate: 2 thread-local cases (local + heap-escaping-but-not-
      thread-crossing — the latter shows thread-locality is derived from the
      call-graph signal, not from heap-escape alone).

    Engines dispatched:
      case_analysis (PRIMARY —
        section_08::verify_rl19_thread_local_nonatomic; thread-local
        atomicity enumeration; emits Fail on a misclassification or an atomic
        selection for a thread-local value)
      rc_counting (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL
        row)
      refinement (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL
        row)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_08 case_analysis engine discharges RL-19 via thread-local atomicity (a value whose escape paths never cross a thread boundary -> non-atomic RC), confirming thread-locality is derived from Locality + call-graph (a HeapEscaping value not crossing a thread boundary is still thread-local), grounded in RL-18a Locality-SSOT + realize/decide.rs Locality consumption
